+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+This contract defines the registry boundary for model-supplied tool input before a consumer executor receives it.
+
+## Contract
+
+1. `ToolRegistry.execute` validates required properties, declared types and enums against the registered JSON Schema before executing, returns a descriptive `ToolResponse` for invalid input without executing, and reports property paths and constraints without input values in either results or logs; valid input, including unknown keys, is delivered unchanged exactly once with its context, without coercion or defaults, while an unknown tool still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects malformed tool input privately and passes valid input unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+2. Static schemas compile at registration, an uncompilable schema throws an error naming the tool at registration, and the compiled schema is reused across ten executions ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L93)).
+3. Function-valued definitions resolve on each execution and validate against the current schema, with compilation cached by resolved schema object identity rather than by tool name ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition and caches each resolved schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L130)).
+
+## Integration and delivery
+
+A validation rejection is a tool result for the model to correct within the existing five-round budget; it must not become a transport exception. The execute doc comment links here in one line. README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md describe rejection results and unchanged extra properties. The validator belongs in runtime dependencies. Delivery includes a MINOR version bump and a consumer-facing changelog and migration note explaining that executors no longer receive malformed input to produce their own errors.
